+{"type":"thought","data":"The SQLite foreign key constraints look solid on paper, but I need to flag a couple of gotchas before we commit to this schema."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFirst, SQLite’s default FK behavior is “RESTRICT” by default, which means it will reject the deletes if any child rows still exist."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" That’s exactly what we want here, but we have to make sure we’re enabling it explicitly:\n\n```sql\nPRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;\n```\n\nSecond, IndexedDB has no FK enforcement at all, so the same delete order is purely semantic there."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" That’s fine, but we should document it clearly in the adapter layer so the browser implementation doesn ’t accidentally try to rely on FKs."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThird, the crash-observer pattern you’re referencing from D."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"109b is the right model: keep the production path clean and only wire up the test-only observer for the new named edges (`after-floor-rewrite`, `after-promotion-delete`, etc.)."}
