+{"type":"thought","data":"The core issue here seems to be ensuring that all these storage layers (IndexedDB, SQLite, and the in-memory fallback) stay consistent with the durability plan—especially around transaction boundaries, auto-commit risks, and how promotion data is handled in the memory store."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFor the IndexedDB side, the cursor-based approach to scan generations, promotions, and blobs in one transaction looks solid."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" It avoids the auto-commit trap by keeping everything inside the live transaction, and awaiting the requests should keep it safe."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe memory store’s `promoted` Set is a quick win for enumeration, but we’ll need to make sure it’s queryable enough for 100% coverage of promotion rows."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" Same for the global blobs—iterating object generation closures plus the promoted set should cover the remaining references."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nOn the SQLite side, the nested BEGIN IMMEDIATE pattern should serialize nicely via locks, so maintenance and normal ops won’t race."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe TransitionOwner mutation and the latchIntegrityFailure call are both authorized, and the error-type split (StoreResult vs."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" custom AHE_RECLAMATION_*) keeps maintenance isolated."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe FK backstop in SQLite is a nice safety net—if the remaining-reference calc is off, a DELETE will either throw SUBSTRATE_FAILURE or fail the change-count check, both 100% correct."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFor the browser Playwright side, we can reuse the existing IDB abort-at-named-edges pattern from D."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"109b, and the generation record structure (objectId + generationId + record bytes) should map cleanly to the keyPath."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nI think the only real unknowns left are confirming that create MemoryAheDurableStore is the only factory and that the storage package exports don’t accidentally add adapter commands."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" Once those are locked down, the plan should be implementable without surprises."}
