+{"type":"thought","data":"The plan is clear: we should stick with the package-owned test-only crash observer (the existing AHE SIGKILL pattern) rather than the child-process monkey-patch from D."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"109b."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" That keeps everything inside the production maintenance code, which is exactly what the D."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"109c spec requires."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nThe current `Sqlite CrashCheckpoint` type already covers the edges we need (`after-commit`, `before-commit`), so we can extend it with a new operation kind like `reclaimClosedEpoch` or just use the existing `after-statement` with a semantic statement name."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" But the cleaner path is to give maintenance its own observer type that only knows about the named edges (`after-floor-rewrite`, `after-promotion-delete`, etc.)."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" That avoids polluting the ordinary mutation type with maintenance-specific edges."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nFor the IDB side, the getAll() and delete() patterns you described are solid."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" The key is to count first (cursor or getAll) before deleting so we can detect “count mismatch” and abort cleanly."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" SQLite’s `changes()` after a DELETE is perfect for the same reason."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nMemory durability is the trickier part."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" We cannot rely on the public memory API to build an Adopted generation because `promoteReference` returns `DURABILITY_UNAVAILABLE`."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" The tests will need to use the internal `memory test control` (the one already used in adapter tests) to seed real `TransitionOwner` states."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" That’s already planned, so we just need to expose the owner via a WeakMap registration at construction time or add a package-internal getter."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" Either way it’s internal, so no public API change."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nSQLite filename and browser database name pins are fine as-is; we’re not changing how the files are selected."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nNine-store authority is already correct, and the vote stores being separate means no deadlock risk with AHE reclamation transactions."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nDiscarded promotions via `discardGeneration` in the adapter look good too it only touches objects and generations, so partial promotion sets are allowed, which matches the plan."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" The conservative “retain too much” behavior for corrupt Complete-then-discarded cases is acceptable."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nOverall, everything is feasible without touching production configuration, dependencies, or runtime behavior."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" The only GREEN changes are inside the maintenance path and the 129-row page limit is handled by reusing the existing internal paging loop for full scans."}
+{"type":"thought","data":" We should add a >129 generation mutant to RED to make sure the full-scan path is exercised, but that’s a small addition."}
+{"type":"thought","data":"\n\nI think we’re good to move forward with the package-owned observer approach."}
