rove lock-mode equivalence.\n   116\t6. [D.109f differential exit](slices/05-differential-exit.md): ≥100-epoch\n   117\t   archival-versus-compacted equivalence, raw-dependency audit, crash/reopen,\n   118\t   and complete enumerated-structure census.\n   119\t\n   120\t## Sacred contracts\n   121\t\n   122\t- The active AHE head and every referenced byte remain complete and recoverable.\n   123\t- Exactly the two immediate rollback ancestors reached by following\n   124\t  `baseExpectedHead` twice from the active adopted generation remain complete\n   125\t  after every AHE reclamation. Both generation rows and every blob in both\n   126\t  closures must exist. Two other countable superseded generations never satisfy\n   127\t  this rule. Random generation identifiers never imply chronological order;\n   128\t  the verified lineage supplies exact identities.\n   129\t- Generation-row reclamation preserves the current parent-presence invariant.\n   130\t  In the same owner transaction that deletes a complete older ancestry prefix,\n   131\t  rewrite only the oldest retained rollback ancestor's `baseExpectedHead` to\n   132\t  the existing `{ kind: \"none\", objectId }` form. Its generation identity,\n   133\t  revision-bearing descendants, closure digest, closure, state, and bytes are\n   134\t  otherwise unchanged. The transaction refuses if any surviving row other than\n   135\t  that exact floor points into the deletion set, if the deletion set is not the\n   136\t  complete connected prefix below the floor, or if post-state lineage has a\n   137\t  dangling parent. This is local metadata compaction, not a wire or digest\n   138\t  change.\n   139\t- An old-epoch issuance row is deletable only when its canonical preimage is\n   140\t  valid, epoch-bound, paired, and `published`. A `pending`, malformed,\n   141\t  one-sided, foreign-digest, or unreadable row blocks that owner with no writes.\n   142\t- The issuance owner retains one monotone per-scope pruning watermark equal to\n   143\t  the inclusive last deleted `authorSequence`, in the same transaction that\n   144\t  removes a complete published prefix. Terminal classification reads the row\n   145\t  and watermark in one owner transaction. Consumed-but-absent addresses at or\n   146\t  below that watermark are `pruned`, never corruption;\n   147\t  a late acknowledgement receives exact non-poisoning\n   148\t  `ISSUANCE_RECORD_PRUNED` rather than an unverified exact-digest success.\n   149\t- Local-only availability requires the adopted local snapshot and exact\n   150\t  equality with frozen availability-policy digest\n   151\t  `53775c5c1ee01e346f588966d6e7acb876df2bd8b2abcbe2b2591f216f7d4d9b`.\n   152\t  Phase 6b never decodes policy bytes. Any other digest retains all data until\n   153\t  Phase 7b owns policy grammar. Mirror receipt verification remains unavailable\n   154\t  until 7b-r and cannot be fabricated in 6b.\n   155\t- Runtime reclamation consumes exact durable receipts and cannot reconstruct\n   156\t  them from current memory.\n   157\t- Advisory browser ownership affects who attempts work, never which bytes are\n   158\t  eligible. Locks on, off, unavailable, rejected, timed out, and takeover yield\n   159\t  the same eventual eligible deletion set.\n   160\t- A cleanup stage may fail by retaining too much; it must never fail by deleting\n   161\t  too much.\n   162\t- Until 7b-r supplies authenticated rollback release, neither of the two\n   163\t  generations counted toward the committed minimum is deletable. The release\n   164\t  conjunction member is vacuous only for older superseded generations beyond\n   165\t  that protected pair.\n   166\t- Phase 6b preserves both the Discord and MMORPG golden paths and enables\n   167\t  neither; D.109f's archival-versus-compacted equivalence list is the proof\n   168\t  obligation.\n   169\t\n   170\t## Review and evidence\n   171\t\n   172\tEach slice follows the prospective D.108e4 review policy: one bounded\n   173\tGrok/Kimi-high-100/Opus plan review where required, deterministic RED, narrow\n   174\tGREEN plus focused/static/retained gates, then one final review over the signed\n   175\tplan/RED/GREEN history. High-risk deletion, schema, scheduling, or threshold\n   176\tchanges explicitly receive the review needed for that risk. Mechanical checks\n   177\town path sets, source shape, result counts, error codes, hashes, manifests,\n   178\tsigned commits, pushed refs, protected paths, stashes, ports, and processes.\n   179\t\n   180\t## Refactor-clean audit\n   181\t\n   182\t- There is one cleanup planner, not per-backend eligibility logic.\n   183\t- There is one physical owner for each byte class; the orchestrator never\n   184\t  reaches into native IDB/SQLite handles.\n   185\t- Existing mandatory `AheDurableStore` and `DurableIssuanceStore` interfaces\n   186\t  remain unchanged. Node/browser adapters expose separate identity-gated\n   187\t  package maintenance capabilities resolved only from their genuine concrete\n   188\t  store instances; ordinary stubs cannot mint deletion authority.\n   189\t- The Phase-5c lock runner is extracted once and the vote dispatcher migrates\n   190\t  to it before cleanup uses it; no compatibility wrapper remains.\n   191\t- Durable receipts are stage results, not a second truth store or permanent\n   192\t  shadow metadata model.\n   193\t- The AHE receipt records the exact lineage floor, its former parent, and the\n   194\t  deleted prefix. It does not authorize a later rewrite; every run rechecks the\n   195\t  current complete graph transactionally.\n   196\t- Public product APIs remain unchanged unless a later slice explicitly proves\n   197\t  an unavoidable package contract change and reviews it before RED.\n   198\t  D.109b’s addition of `ISSUANCE_RECORD_PRUNED` to the closed issuance error\n   199\t  union and its required pruning-watermark member in the public terminal\n   200\t  observation are one demonstrated exception: deleted digest evidence makes\n   201\t  both success and corruption false.\n   202\t\n   203\t## One-off advisory review\n   204\t\n   205\tThe expressly authorized Fable 5/high read-only review used session\n   206\t`69ab32d6-9d07-4f38-953a-600d457b5320` and returned `CHANGES_REQUIRED` with two\n   207\tP1 and two P2 findings. Result text SHA-256 was\n   208\t`10dd88c2633239de76abb69158ba21899408dcf797d0425efe6d3a288becaefc`.\n   209\tThis corrected plan adopts the two P1s: a durable issuance pruning watermark\n   210\twith non-poisoning pruned classification, and exact digest equality for the\n   211\tfrozen local-only availability profile without policy decoding. It also adopts\n   212\tthe P2s by naming separate identity-gated maintenance capabilities and a full\n   213\tcross-object remaining-closure scan before global blob deletion. The reviewer\n   214\tapproved the staged owner topology, D.109a’s causal value, slice order, runtime\n   215\treuse, and Phase-5c advisory scheduling reuse. This one-off review is complete\n   216\tand must not be relaunched.\n"}],"tool_call_id":"tool_geSMF5pPv8awOxICJ5We882L"}
+{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system>100 lines read from file starting from line 1. Total lines in file: 100. End of file reached.</system>"},{"type":"text","text":"     1\t# D.109a — Closed-Epoch Cleanup Eligibility\n     2\t\n     3\t## Question\n     4\t\n     5\tCan one package-internal owner deterministically refuse unsafe cleanup before\n     6\tany physical store is allowed to mutate?\n     7\t\n     8\t## Seam\n     9\t\n    10\tAdd one package-internal `@ts-drp/node` cleanup-planning module. It accepts\n    11\talready verified, detached facts from the existing close/adoption owners and\n    12\treturns either an immutable stage plan or one closed refusal code. It exposes\n    13\tno package export and performs no I/O or deletion.\n    14\t\n    15\tThe plan identifies, by exact value rather than ordering inference:\n    16\t\n    17\t- object and closed epoch;\n    18\t- verified commit-QC and adopted-head bindings;\n    19\t- expected current head/revision;\n    20\t- active generation and exactly the two complete rollback generations reached\n    21\t  by following `baseExpectedHead` twice from that active adopted generation;\n    22\t- the exact oldest-retained lineage floor, its expected original base (present\n    23\t  when an older prefix exists), and the complete connected older prefix eligible\n    24\t  for atomic floor normalization and deletion;\n    25\t- adopted local snapshot plus the adopted CutValue’s exact\n    26\t  `availabilityPolicyDigest`;\n    27\t- the issuance scope and upper epoch boundary to classify; and\n    28\t- exact durable identities later stages must recheck.\n    29\t\n    30\t## RED\n    31\t\n    32\tOne tests-only owner drives the genuine Phase-6a close/adoption material into\n    33\tthe missing module and requires:\n    34\t\n    35\t- a complete local-only positive control with the active generation plus both\n    36\t  immediate `baseExpectedHead` rollback ancestors and all three closures;\n    37\t- refusal for missing/unverified QC, non-adopted or mismatched head, fewer than\n    38\t  two distinct usable rollbacks, a wrong-but-countable pair of non-ancestor\n    39\t  superseded generations, either missing ancestor row or incomplete ancestor\n    40\t  closure, missing local snapshot, mismatched policy, incomplete outbox\n    41\t  classification, malformed/duplicate identities, and stale expected revision;\n    42\t- refusal when the proposed older deletion set is gapped, when any surviving\n    43\t  generation other than the exact floor points into it, or when simulating the\n    44\t  floor's sole `baseExpectedHead` normalization still leaves a dangling parent;\n    45\t- a causal mutant proving that deleting the parent of the oldest retained\n    46\t  ancestor without that exact normalization makes subsequent creator adoption\n    47\t  return `chain-invalid`;\n    48\t- permutation invariance of unordered facts;\n    49\t- detached immutable output;\n    50\t- exact refusal precedence; and\n    51\t- source guards proving zero calls to delete/clear/discard and no exported API.\n    52\t\n    53\tThe RED must fail only because the package-internal planner and its exact\n    54\tclosed result union do not yet exist. Existing Phase-6a retained tests stay\n    55\tgreen.\n    56\t\n    57\t## GREEN\n    58\t\n    59\tImplement only validation, canonical ordering, copying, and immutable planning.\n    60\tReuse existing canonical bytes/digests and Phase-6a fact owners. The only\n    61\taccepted availability policy is exact equality with literal digest\n    62\t`53775c5c1ee01e346f588966d6e7acb876df2bd8b2abcbe2b2591f216f7d4d9b`,\n    63\tindependently derived as `hashDomain(\"ts-drp/availability-policy/v3\", bytes)`\n    64\tover canonical bytes\n    65\t`080405046d6f6465050a6c6f63616c2d6f6e6c79050e6d696e4c6f63616c436f70696573030205116d696e4d6972726f725265636569707473030005166d696e526f6c6c6261636b47656e65726174696f6e730304`.\n    66\tThe planner never accepts or decodes policy bytes; any other digest receives a\n    67\tclosed refusal and retains data for Phase 7b. Do not verify signatures again,\n    68\topen a store, add schema, schedule work, or reclaim memory.\n    69\t\n    70\tThe immutable positive result carries an exact lineage-floor rewrite intent:\n    71\tthe floor generation identity, its expected original base, the existing no-head\n    72\treplacement scoped to the same object, and the complete older prefix. D.109a\n    73\tonly simulates the post-state graph and never mutates a record.\n    74\tWhen the floor is already the original no-head generation, the expected base is\n    75\tthat existing no-head value, the deletion prefix is empty, and the later stage\n    76\tis an idempotent no-op rather than a fabricated rewrite.\n    77\t\n    78\t## Acceptance\n    79\t\n    80\t- Focused RED/GREEN executes once per color with an exact test count and exact\n    81\t  failure token at RED.\n    82\t- Node/object/storage affected typechecks, exact-owner lint/format/diff, and\n    83\t  retained Phase-6a semantic tests pass.\n    84\t- The changed production path set is the one internal planner only; the tests\n    85\t  and plan/evidence paths are enumerated separately.\n    86\t- A source-shape check proves no delete-like operation and no package export.\n    87\t\n    88\tThe frozen owner is\n    89\t`tests/phase-6b-cleanup-eligibility-red.test.ts`; its sole GREEN source is\n    90\t`packages/node/src/internal/closed-epoch-cleanup.ts`. The closed refusal\n    91\tprecedence is `D109A_QC_INVALID`, `D109A_ADOPTION_INVALID`,\n    92\t`D109A_HEAD_MISMATCH`, `D109A_REVISION_STALE`, `D109A_IDENTITY_INVALID`,\n    93\t`D109A_LINEAGE_INVALID`, `D109A_ROLLBACK_INSUFFICIENT`,\n    94\t`D109A_SNAPSHOT_MISSING`, `D109A_POLICY_UNSUPPORTED`, then\n    95\t`D109A_OUTBOX_INCOMPLETE`.\n    96\t\n    97\t## Handoff\n    98\t\n    99\tD.109b may consume the immutable plan only after its own store-local\n   100\ttransaction revalidates the issuance facts. This slice authorizes no deletion.\n"}],"tool_call_id":"tool_2xeLL7F20ejAWTrQqs7reHzk"}
