+{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system>337 lines read from file starting from line 1. Total lines in file: 337. End of file reached.</system>"},{"type":"text","text":"     1\t# D.109c — AHE Generation and Blob Reclamation\n     2\t\n     3\t## Status and inherited anchors\n     4\t\n     5\tD.109c starts only after signed/pushed D.109b closure\n     6\t`2afadbe682261bdb311a5cb64f6f42d86ed7330b`. D.109a's planner and D.109b's\n     7\tissuance deletion remain accepted, immutable prerequisites. This slice changes\n     8\tonly AHE physical ownership. It authorizes no runtime reclamation, scheduler,\n     9\tcampaign, threshold, dependency, protocol, wire, digest, QC, adoption,\n    10\tavailability, issuance, snapshot, or product-handle change.\n    11\t\n    12\tThe active formal-review trio is Grok 4.6/high, exact Kimi K3 thinking/high\n    13\twith both `KIMI_LOOP_MAX_STEPS_PER_TURN=100` and\n    14\t`--max-steps-per-turn 100`, and Opus xhigh. Kimi occupies the middle\n    15\texternal-CLI slot; Codex `gpt-5.6-sol` is not a substitute. If Grok cancels,\n    16\tresume that exact session. Fable and collaboration subagents are not\n    17\tauthorized.\n    18\t\n    19\t## Source audit and one-owner seam\n    20\t\n    21\tThe mandatory `AheDurableStore` remains the exact existing 12-key facade:\n    22\t`capabilities` plus `readHead`, `readGenerationPage`,\n    23\t`recoverActiveGeneration`, `getBlob`, `beginGeneration`, `putCachedBlob`,\n    24\t`promoteReference`, `completeGeneration`, `swapHead`, `discardGeneration`, and\n    25\t`close`. D.109c does not add a thirteenth key.\n    26\t\n    27\tCurrent physical facts are:\n    28\t\n    29\t- memory owns objects, generation rows, global blobs, and promotion evidence in\n    30\t  one synchronous `TransitionOwner`;\n    31\t- Node owns exact `objects`, `generations`, `blobs`, and `promotions` SQLite\n    32\t  tables in the caller-selected file under WAL/FULL and foreign keys;\n    33\t- browser owns the same four AHE stores inside the existing Phase-5e IndexedDB\n    34\t  version-3 database. D.109c changes neither database name, schema version,\n    35\t  store/table/key path, nor unrelated vote/evidence stores;\n    36\t- blob identity is global by digest, not object-local, and neither persisted\n    37\t  backend has a reverse index;\n    38\t- creator adoption rejects every surviving generation whose `present`\n    39\t  `baseExpectedHead` parent row is missing. Deleting an older prefix without\n    40\t  rewriting the retained floor is therefore a demonstrated recovery defect.\n    41\t\n    42\tThere is one shared `@ts-drp/storage/maintenance` owner for the closed request,\n    43\treceipt/error types, copying, canonical-generation validation, lineage graph\n    44\tclassification, and remaining-reference calculation. Memory registers its\n    45\tcapability through a package-private identity registry. Node and browser each\n    46\tadd only `./maintenance`, backed by a module-private `WeakMap` keyed by the\n    47\texact facade their existing factory returned. Copies, proxies, structural\n    48\tlookalikes, and cross-backend facades resolve to `undefined`. Package roots and\n    49\tordinary factory modules do not re-export maintenance.\n    50\t\n    51\tBackend transactions remain the only physical mutation owners. No generic\n    52\tadapter command, `AheDurableStore` method, public runtime handle, reverse-index\n    53\tschema, receipt shadow table, or cross-database transaction is added.\n    54\t\n    55\t## Closed maintenance contract\n    56\t\n    57\tThe one method is:\n    58\t\n    59\t```text\n    60\treclaimClosedEpoch(input: unknown): Promise<AheReclamationReceipt>\n    61\t```\n    62\t\n    63\tThe captured exact input has only:\n    64\t\n    65\t```text\n    66\t{\n    67\t  activeGenerationId,\n    68\t  availabilityPolicyDigest,\n    69\t  closedEpoch,\n    70\t  expectedHead,\n    71\t  lineageFloor: {\n    72\t    deleteGenerationIds,\n    73\t    expectedBaseExpectedHead,\n    74\t    generationId,\n    75\t    replacementBaseExpectedHead\n    76\t  },\n    77\t  objectId,\n    78\t  rollbackGenerationIds\n    79\t}\n    80\t```\n    81\t\n    82\tIt is the detached AHE subset of one successful D.109a plan. The availability\n    83\tdigest must be the frozen local-only digest\n    84\t`53775c5c1ee01e346f588966d6e7acb876df2bd8b2abcbe2b2591f216f7d4d9b`;\n    85\tD.109c compares it but never decodes policy bytes. The expected head is\n    86\t`present`; active, both rollback, floor, and deletion identities are valid,\n    87\tdistinct where required, exact closed records; rollback order is immediate\n    88\tparent then grandparent; deletion identities have no duplicates; replacement\n    89\tis exactly `{ kind: \"none\", objectId }`; and an empty deletion list is valid\n    90\tonly when the expected floor parent is already that same no-head value.\n    91\tAccessors, inherited fields, symbols, sparse arrays, shared buffers, aliases,\n    92\textra fields, and impossible relationships fail before transaction work.\n    93\t\n    94\tSuccess returns a detached deeply frozen receipt with exact keys:\n    95\t\n    96\t```text\n    97\t{\n    98\t  activeGenerationId,\n    99\t  availabilityPolicyDigest,\n   100\t  closedEpoch,\n   101\t  deletedBlobDigests,\n   102\t  deletedGenerationIds,\n   103\t  deletedPromotionCount,\n   104\t  expectedHead,\n   105\t  floor: {\n   106\t    expectedFormerBaseExpectedHead,\n   107\t    generationId,\n   108\t    normalizedThisCall,\n   109\t    replacementBaseExpectedHead\n   110\t  },\n   111\t  objectId,\n   112\t  reclaimedGenerationIds,\n   113\t  rollbackGenerationIds\n   114\t}\n   115\t```\n   116\t\n   117\t`reclaimedGenerationIds` is the exact requested older prefix proven absent at\n   118\tcommit. `deletedGenerationIds`, `deletedPromotionCount`, and\n   119\t`deletedBlobDigests` describe writes performed by this call. A lost-receipt\n   120\treplay has the same reclaimed prefix, `normalizedThisCall: false`, and empty\n   121\tactual-deletion fields. No receipt contains blob bytes, closure bytes, QC,\n   122\tsignatures, snapshot bytes, runtime authority, or a future-deletion grant.\n   123\t\n   124\tFailures are frozen errors with one of exactly:\n   125\t\n   126\t- `AHE_RECLAMATION_INVALID_ARGUMENT`: malformed or internally impossible\n   127\t  caller input; never poisons;\n   128\t- `AHE_RECLAMATION_RETRY_REQUIRED`: a well-formed head, revision, generation,\n   129\t  floor, branch, or selected-set observation changed since planning; zero\n   130\t  writes and no poison;\n   131\t- `AHE_RECLAMATION_CORRUPT`: malformed/unreadable native bytes, key/record\n   132\t  mismatch, broken retained closure/promotion/blob evidence, impossible partial\n   133\t  replay, or a malformed global remaining-reference row; zero committed writes\n   134\t  and the ordinary store latches poison;\n   135\t- `AHE_RECLAMATION_STORE_CLOSED` and `AHE_RECLAMATION_STORE_POISONED`: exact\n   136\t  lifecycle precedence;\n   137\t- `AHE_RECLAMATION_SUBSTRATE_FAILURE`: a contained native failure with cause;\n   138\t  no false success.\n   139\t\n   140\tNo error exposes persisted bytes. Every backend returns asynchronous rejection,\n   141\tnever a backend-specific synchronous throw.\n   142\t\n   143\t## Transactional algorithm\n   144\t\n   145\tOne memory critical section, SQLite `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, or strict IndexedDB\n   146\t`readwrite` transaction over the four AHE stores performs this exact order:\n   147\t\n   148\t1. Recheck lifecycle and decode the target object's head. A different valid\n   149\t   head/revision is retry; malformed persisted head is corruption.\n   150\t2. Enumerate and canonically decode every target generation row. Rebuild the\n   151\t   chain from expected head → active → immediate rollback → second rollback →\n   152\t   complete older prefix. Generation IDs are never sorted as chronology.\n   153\t3. Require active `Adopted`; both rollback rows and every selected prefix row\n   154\t   `Superseded`; exact head/closure-digest/revision links; canonical nonempty\n   155\t   digest-sorted closures; and exact equality with the requested active,\n   156\t   rollback, floor, former-parent, and deletion identities. Any additional\n   157\t   target generation row makes the plan stale rather than silently deleting it.\n   158\t4. Verify active and both rollback closures remain complete: every referenced\n   159\t   blob exists with exact byte length/digest and every promotion exists. Verify\n   160\t   selected superseded rows' complete promotion/blob evidence before treating\n   161\t   their references as newly reclaimable candidates.\n   162\t5. Enumerate every generation record across every object and every promotion\n   163\t   row in the database. Decode/bind each generation to its physical key. Every\n   164\t   promotion must bind to an existing generation and a digest in that\n   165\t   generation's closure. Any malformed remaining row aborts; omission cannot\n   166\t   be interpreted as “unreferenced.” `Staged` and `Discarded` rows may have a\n   167\t   promotion subset because discard is legal before completion; only\n   168\t   `Complete`, `Adopted`, and `Superseded` rows require complete promotion\n   169\t   sets.\n   170\t6. Reject cycles, gaps, wrong floor/parent, any surviving non-floor edge into\n   171\t   the selected prefix, any selected row outside the complete connected prefix,\n   172\t   or any simulated post-state dangling `present` parent.\n   173\t7. For a nonempty fresh prefix, rewrite only the second rollback/floor record's\n   174\t   `baseExpectedHead` from the exact expected parent to the existing no-head\n   175\t   form. Preserve every other generation field and re-encode canonical storage\n   176\t   v1 bytes. Exact one-row update is required.\n   177\t8. Delete exactly all promotions owned by the selected prefix, then exactly the\n   178\t   selected generation rows. Count mismatch aborts.\n   179\t9. From the selected closures, delete a candidate global blob only when no\n   180\t   remaining generation closure across any object and no remaining promotion\n   181\t   references its digest. Shared and unrelated-object blobs remain. Exact\n   182\t   delete counts are checked.\n   183\t10. Reread/simulate the resulting target graph: expected head, active, both\n   184\t    rollback closures, normalized floor, no selected rows/promotions, and no\n   185\t    dangling parent must all hold before commit. Then return the frozen receipt.\n   186\t\n   187\tNo await or externally supplied callback may split the memory critical section.\n   188\tNode executes no callback inside the transaction except the package-owned\n   189\ttest-only crash observer. Browser issues every cursor/request from the one live\n   190\ttransaction and performs no unrelated asynchronous work that could auto-commit\n   191\tit.\n   192\t\n   193\t## Idempotence and concurrency\n   194\t\n   195\t- An initially empty prefix with a no-head floor is a no-write success.\n   196\t- A lost-receipt replay is accepted only when every requested prefix row and\n   197\t  promotion is absent, the exact floor is already no-head, the head/active/two\n   198\t  rollback graph still matches, and retained closure evidence is complete.\n   199\t- All-present plus expected former parent is the only fresh mutable state.\n   200\t  Any mixed present/absent prefix, already-normalized floor with a surviving\n   201\t  selected row, or absent selected row with the old floor still present is\n   202\t  corruption, never a guessed replay.\n   203\t- A second live handle that changes any selected fact before lock acquisition\n   204\t  receives retry or observes the committed idempotent state; it cannot combine\n   205\t  old classification with new writes.\n   206\t- Closing or poisoning during admission cannot publish a receipt. A failed\n   207\t  transaction retains the prior recovery certificate and bytes; a committed\n   208\t  floor rewrite does not change the head fingerprint or active closure.\n   209\t\n   210\t## Deterministic RED\n   211\t\n   212\tRED adds tests/fixtures/config only. Production source, package manifests,\n   213\tschemas, lockfile, dependencies, thresholds, and runtime code remain\n   214\tbyte-identical to D.109b closure.\n   215\t\n   216\tThe exact new RED path roster is:\n   217\t\n   218\t1. `tests/fixtures/phase-6b/ahe-reclamation-contract.ts`\n   219\t2. `tests/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-red.test.ts`\n   220\t3. `packages/storage-node/tests/fixtures/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-child.mjs`\n   221\t4. `packages/storage-node/tests/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-red.test.ts`\n   222\t5. `packages/storage-browser/playwright.phase-6b-ahe-reclamation.config.ts`\n   223\t6. `packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-global-setup.ts`\n   224\t7. `packages/storage-browser/tests/assets/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-entry.ts`\n   225\t8. `packages/storage-browser/tests/assets/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-worker.ts`\n   226\t9. `packages/storage-browser/tests/phase-6b-ahe-reclamation-red.pw.ts`\n   227\t\n   228\tThe focused Vitest selection covers the shared/memory and genuine Node owners;\n   229\tthe focused Playwright selection is exactly one file and the frozen Chromium\n   230\ttests. Before GREEN, controls pass and semantic bodies skip behind exact\n   231\treadiness predicates; failures are only\n   232\t`D109C_SHARED_MAINTENANCE_MISSING`, `D109C_NODE_MAINTENANCE_MISSING`, and\n   233\t`D109C_BROWSER_MAINTENANCE_MISSING`. Any module-resolution, build, server,\n   234\tfixture, selected-count, top-level, or different-token failure invalidates RED.\n   235\t\n   236\tThe frozen semantic roster covers:\n   237\t\n   238\t- exact facade/export census and identity denial for copy/proxy/fake/\n   239\t  cross-backend values;\n   240\t- detached closed input, frozen receipt/error, exact error-key/code registry,\n   241\t  and lifecycle precedence;\n   242\t- genuine five-generation positive control retaining active plus its two\n   243\t  immediate ancestors, normalizing only the second rollback, deleting the two\n   244\t  older connected rows/promotions, and preserving active/rollback bytes;\n   245\t- empty-prefix success, lost-receipt replay, two-live-handle serialization,\n   246\t  reopen, and a subsequent genuine creator-adoption commit;\n   247\t- stale/different head or revision, active mismatch, insufficient rollback,\n   248\t  wrong-but-countable rollback pair, duplicate identity, changed closure/state,\n   249\t  wrong floor, wrong former parent, gap, cycle, alternate surviving branch,\n   250\t  extra target row, and simulated dangling post-state;\n   251\t- missing/corrupt retained blob, missing/extra/wrong promotion, malformed\n   252\t  target or unrelated generation bytes, key/record mismatch, and partial\n   253\t  replay; every corrupt case performs zero committed writes and poisons;\n   254\t- shared blobs within the retained set and across an unrelated object,\n   255\t  candidate-only blob deletion, unrelated orphan retention, and full global\n   256\t  remaining-generation plus promotion scanning;\n   257\t- injected floor-update, promotion-delete, generation-delete, and blob-delete\n   258\t  count mismatches, each rolling back the complete transaction;\n   259\t- Node hard `SIGKILL` at `after-floor-rewrite`,\n   260\t  `after-promotion-delete`, `after-generation-delete`, `after-blob-delete`,\n   261\t  `before-commit`, and `after-commit`; reopen must be old XOR complete-new;\n   262\t- Chromium worker termination/transaction abort at the corresponding live-IDB\n   263\t  stages, with reopen old XOR complete-new and no partial floor/prefix/blob\n   264\t  combination.\n   265\t\n   266\tRED also retains the D.109a planner positive/refusal matrix and its dangling-\n   267\tparent oracle. It does not claim production behavior for skipped semantics and\n   268\tdoes not run a retained campaign.\n   269\t\n   270\t## GREEN implementation batches\n   271\t\n   272\tOne D.109c GREEN checkpoint uses two diagnostic batches without an intermediate\n   273\tcommit or model review:\n   274\t\n   275\t1. **Shared contract and memory owner.** Add the maintenance types, classifier,\n   276\t   private registry, `TransitionOwner` mutation, memory test control, exact\n   277\t   package subpath, and run the focused shared/memory file once.\n   278\t2. **Native owners.** Add Node and browser identity registries, transactions,\n   279\t   test-only fault edges, package subpaths, and run the focused Node and browser\n   280\t   commands once before the retained suites.\n   281\t\n   282\tIf either focused run reports a code/token outside its frozen matrix, stop and\n   283\tdiagnose rather than folding another concept into the batch. Before final\n   284\treview, apply `refactor-clean`: one shared graph classifier, one backend\n   285\ttransaction per physical owner, no duplicate lineage walker, no compatibility\n   286\twrapper, and no temporary export left behind.\n   287\t\n   288\t## GREEN and retained gates\n   289\t\n   290\tGREEN must prove all focused assertions with no skip, failure, flaky result,\n   291\tor top-level error, then run:\n   292\t\n   293\t- affected `@ts-drp/storage`, `storage-node`, `storage-browser`, and `node`\n   294\t  builds plus source-only typechecks;\n   295\t- exact-owner ESLint, Prettier, `git diff --check`, package/root/factory export\n   296\t  census, schema/version/name source shape, no generic adapter-command growth,\n   297\t  and changed-path custody;\n   298\t- retained storage codecs, memory/state-machine, adapter facade, bounded reads,\n   299\t  taxonomy/poison, recovery authority/memory-bound, Node SQLite contract/\n   300\t  SIGKILL/lifecycle, browser schema/adapter/recovery/process-death, D.109a\n   301\t  planner, and Phase-6a creator adoption/reopen tests;\n   302\t- a self-excluding evidence manifest covering complete reporter JSON, stdout,\n   303\t  stderr, child/worker observations, commands, hashes, and dispositions;\n   304\t- signature, pushed-ref equality, protected paths, 26 stashes, fixed ports,\n   305\t  and no conflicting ts-drp reviewer/test/profiler process.\n   306\t\n   307\tThe Node file path, four-table DDL, WAL/FULL/foreign-key policy, browser\n   308\tdatabase name and version 3, nine-store authority, four AHE key paths, storage\n   309\tv1 codecs, D.109a planner result, and both creator parent-presence predicates\n   310\tare source pins. Directly affected hashes may change only for the frozen owner\n   311\tpaths; unrelated source drift stops the slice.\n   312\t\n   313\t## Review and stop conditions\n   314\t\n   315\tThis is high-risk because it authorizes physical generation/blob deletion and\n   316\tchanges crash behavior. Sign and push this bounded plan, then run one\n   317\tGrok/Kimi/Opus plan review. Only P0/P1 blocks; disposition P2 without recursive\n   318\tprose review. Permit at most one confirmation if a P0/P1 correction changes\n   319\tscope, causal RED behavior, or a hard acceptance gate. Deterministic RED gets\n   320\tno separate full model round. Sign/push GREEN, then run the sole final\n   321\tGrok/Kimi/Opus review over plan → RED → GREEN history. Only P0/P1 blocks\n   322\tclosure.\n   323\t\n   324\tStop and reslice rather than widen scope if safe implementation requires a\n   325\tschema/reverse index, mandatory facade change, product/runtime API, dependency,\n   326\tthreshold, workload, protocol/wire/digest/QC/adoption/availability change, or\n   327\tcross-database authority. D.109c runs no retained campaign. D.109d remains\n   328\tunopened until D.109c's signed GREEN evidence and final review are complete.\n   329\t\n   330\t## Human-verifiable outcome\n   331\t\n   332\tThe focused evidence must show, in plain data, the head and three retained\n   333\tgeneration records before/after, the exact floor-parent rewrite, exact removed\n   334\tprefix/promotions, shared-versus-deleted blob digests, replay receipt, and old\n   335\tXOR complete-new crash observations for Node and Chromium. A reviewer can\n   336\ttherefore decide deletion safety without inferring it from implementation\n   337\tprose.\n"}],"tool_call_id":"tool_FifkvuonSsn4QYgUWTUrGpBv"}
