+{"role":"tool","content":"87479:3. **D.109c AHE reclamation:** a separate identity-gated maintenance capability\n87506:Because current adoption validates that every present parent has a row, a D.109c\n87563:are not widened. D.109b and D.109c use separate package maintenance\n87676:D.109c rechecks the complete graph, normalizes only that floor, deletes the\n87862:   D.109c own those values as explicit transaction inputs when they recheck\n87869:   planner. D.109c owns its explicit owner-transaction refusal matrix and\n87875:   a real nonempty prefix, and D.109c must retain the empty-prefix idempotence,\n88179:blocks D.109b closure. D.109c remains closed until that review is complete.\n88213:D.109b is closed on this signed record. D.109c may begin next. No retained\n88216:#### D.109c AHE-reclamation plan checkpoint\n88218:D.109c is frozen in\n88226:reverse index. D.109c therefore adds no schema, index, database identity,\n88315:unopened and D.109c authorizes no retained campaign.","tool_call_id":"tool_ztMJBlfhj2pbCMMP4nAQFN8M"}
