ect... `Staged` and `Discarded` rows may have a promotion subset\" — that's for *other* objects' generations in the global reference scan. Fine.\n\nOne potential issue: deleting a blob requires \"no remaining generation closure across any object and no remaining promotion references its digest.\" But what about *Staged* generations on *other* objects whose closure references a candidate blob but whose promotion isn't yet recorded? Closure reference counts (\"no remaining generation closure ... references its digest\") — closures are retained regardless of state, so a Staged generation's closure still references the blob; the blob won't be deleted. Good — closure-based protection covers that.\n\nWhat about a blob that was putCachedBlob'd for a staged generation whose generation row was discarded... Discarded generations still exist as rows with closures, so their references still protect. OK.\n\nWhat about blobs not referenced by any generation at all (\"unrelated orphan retention\")? Orphans are never candidates since candidates come only from selected closures. OK.\n\nNow check the memory-store factory and facade freezing for the WeakMap identity registry feasibility: `MemoryAheDurableStore` constructor does `Object.freeze(this)`. Node store — check the factory in storage-node index.ts. Browser — check the browser AHE store factory.","encrypted":null},{"type":"text","text":"Now check the Node factory and browser AHE store factory to verify the identity-registry seam feasibility."}],"tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_ddUFGo41RrYTspqCLx1cviJG","function":{"name":"ReadFile","arguments":"{\"path\": \"/Users/aristotle/Documents/Projects/ts-drp-1/packages/storage-node/src/index.ts\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"tool_qq3xw3a0RllJgnUi6EMfFXDZ","function":{"name":"Shell","arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/aristotle/Documents/Projects/ts-drp-1/packages/storage-browser && ls src/internal && grep -n \\\"createBrowserAheDurableStore\\\\|export function\\\\|export a