+{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"think","think":"Commit is GPG-signed (`G`), parent is exactly the D.109b closure, and it touches only the three plan documents. The branch list shows it's contained in at least one remote branch (`origin/codex/phase3a1b-p6-golden-path` — odd name but it's a pushed ref containing it; actually `git branch -r --contains` printed that one branch; good enough as pushed evidence).\n\nRemaining scrutiny — a couple of deeper correctness checks I want to close out:\n\n1. **Step 10 post-state verification before commit**: In SQLite/IDB you can reread within the transaction. Memory: simulate. ✓.\n\n2. **Requirement 3 wording**: \"the two immediate superseded rollback ancestors\" — the request carries rollbackGenerationIds and revalidates they're the immediate parents via ancestry following (step 2-3). ✓.\n\n3. **Does step 3's \"exact head/closure-digest/revision links\" plus input's expectedHead cover \"exact head/revision\" revalidation (requirement 3)?** Yes.\n\n4. **Anything about the receipt needing `closedEpoch` consistency vs head?** The epoch is carried for receipt/evidence; the store has no epoch notion (AHE store is epoch-agnostic — epochs live in the node layer). Deletion safety rests on lineage/state, not epoch numbers. closedEpoch in input is validated as a safe integer and recorded; it doesn't gate anything in the store. That's fine since D.109a bound the epoch to verified facts. No issue.\n\n5. **Empty-prefix + no-head floor: is `normalizedThisCall: false` and empty deletes the result?** Yes — \"no-write success\". ✓.\n\n6. **The plan's claim that the RED \"retains the D.109a planner positive/refusal matrix and its dangling-parent oracle\"** — retained tests exist (tests/phase-6b-cleanup-eligibility-red.test.ts, now green). ✓.\n\n7. **`packages/storage-browser/playwright.phase-6b-ahe-reclamation.config.ts`** — new playwright config; precedent shows per-slice configs. ✓.\n\n8. **Selected-count and top-level failure invalidation** — mirrors D.109b.\n\nOne more requirement-7 probe: \"controls can run while semantics skip solely behind the three readiness tokens\". In D.109b the browser used an env var `D109B_BROWSER_MAINTENANCE_READY` plus in-test skip with token message. D.109c uses `D109C_*` analogues. ✓.\n\nPotential P2 observations (non-blocking):\n- The slice's semantic roster doesn't explicitly enumerate a mutant for \"replay accepted with a changed head\" distinctly, but \"stale/different head or revision\" covers fresh path; replay requires graph match which is covered by the replay definition. Non-blocking.\n- Receipt exposes deleted blob digests not present in the request — informational; the plan itself demands this for human-verifiable evidence. Not a finding.\n- Memory maintenance is exercisable only via package-internal seeding since memory cannot publicly complete generations; plan budgets \"memory test control\". Not a defect.\n\nI've checked all nine requirements against the source. Everything asserted about seams and feasibility is source-grounded:\n\nReq 1 ✓ (12-key facade verified at types.ts:110-151; WeakMap/registry precedent at node-issuance-store.ts:1075-1151; factories return genuine instances).\nReq 2 ✓ (single shared owner planned; classifier pure, backends own transactions; D.109a plan shape matches input exactly at closed-epoch-cleanup.ts:34-56).\nReq 3 ✓ (revalidation steps 1-3; empty-prefix & replay decidable).\nReq 4 ✓ (steps 4-10; partial promotion allowance matches discardGeneration semantics at transition.ts:585-599 and closure-verifier).\nReq 5 ✓ (closed six-code taxonomy; async rejection; no bytes).\nReq 6 ✓ (TransitionOwner synchronous; BEGIN IMMEDIATE precedent; strict IDB precedent; crash observer infra at create-scaffold.ts:52-61, SIGKILL harness precedent; worker terminate precedent).\nReq 7 ✓ (nine paths, three tokens mirror accepted D.109b pattern; roster comprehensive; no infeasible fixture or missing causal mutant found).\nReq 8 ✓ (two batches, gates, pins, custody, stop/reslice; no runtime reclamation/D.109d/campaign authorized).\nReq 9 ✓ (no schema/index/facade/dependency/protocol change needed: full scans replace reverse index; floor rewrite reuses existing no-head record variant; generation IDs are random, not content digests — creator-close.ts:227-233, validation.ts:91-93).\n\nVerdict: APPROVED, no P0/P1, RED may start.","encrypted":null},{"type":"text","text":"## Review summary\n\nI independently verified the frozen D.109c plan (commit `e2c18898`, GPG-signed, parent exactly the accepted D.109b closure `2afadbe6`, diff touching only the three plan documents) against the current sources. Findings per requirement:\n\n**1. Facade isolation — verified.** `AheDurableStore` is exactly the 12-key facade listed (`packages/storage/src/types.ts:110-151`). The identity-gated maintenance seam is not speculative: D.109b already landed the exact `WeakMap`-keyed resolver pattern (`packages/storage-node/src/internal/node-issuance-store.ts:1075-1151`, `packages/storage-node/src/issuance-maintenance.ts`), factories return genuine concrete instances (`create-scaffold.ts:135`, `idb-adapter.ts:963-971`, `memory.ts:246`), and `./issuance-maintenance` subpaths are the accepted precedent for the planned `./maintenance` subpaths.\n\n**2. One shared owner — verified feasible.** The D.109a plan output (`packages/node/src/internal/closed-epoch-cleanup.ts:34-56`) is field-for-field the claimed D.109c input AHE subset (`activeGenerationId`, `availabilityPolicyDigest`, `closedEpoch`, `expectedHead`, `lineageFloor{deleteGenerationIds, expectedBaseExpectedHead, generationId, replacementBaseExpectedHead}`, `objectId`, `rollbackGenerationIds` tuple). Backends alone own transactions; the shared classifier is pure over transaction-read rows — no duplicate walker or generic adapter command is required, and GREEN's refactor-clean gate pins this.\n\n**3–5. Revalidation, transaction, error partition — coherent.** Algorithm steps 1–10 cover head/revision, ancestry-following (never ID order; generation IDs are random 32-byte hex per `creator-close.ts:227-233` and `validation.ts:91-93`, so the floor rewrite cannot break identity), complete-prefix proof, retained+selected closure/promotion/blob verification, global cross-object decode-scan (replacing the absent reverse index — schema confirmed at `create-scaffold.ts:76-100`, `schema-idb.ts:4-71`: 4 AHE tables/stores, global digest-keyed blobs, no indexes, version 3 / nine stores), exact counts, and post-state checks. `Staged`/`Discarded` partial-promotion allowance matches `discardGeneration` semantics (`transition.ts:585-599`) and the candidate/adopted verifier split. Empty-prefix and lost-receipt replay rules are decidable and match D.109a's empty-prefix contract (`00-eligibility.md:74-76`). The six-code taxonomy, closed-before-poisoned precedence (mirroring `transition.ts:108-112`), poison-on-corrupt, and async-only rejection are implementable fresh.\n\n**6. Atomicity/crash evidence — feasible with existing owners.** Memory's `TransitionOwner` is fully synchronous; Node has `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`/WAL/FULL/foreign-keys plus an existing package-owned crash-observer seam (`create-scaffold.ts:52-61,246,763,785-786`) and SIGKILL child harness precedent (`phase-6b-issuance-retention-red.test.ts:135`); Chromium has strict-durability transactions (`idb-adapter.ts:504-506`) and worker `terminate()`/IDB-death precedent (`phase-2e6-real-process-death-entry.ts`, `phase-5c-seal-vote-schema.pw.ts:197`). New fault edges are budgeted as test-only GREEN instrumentation. The parent-presence defect the floor rewrite closes is real (`creator-adoption.ts:209-218`, `creator-adoption-commit.ts:213-222`), and RED's subsequent-genuine-adoption case is the right oracle.\n\n**7. RED causality — sound.** The nine paths mirror the accepted D.109b eight plus one justified worker asset; the three readiness tokens replicate the accepted skip pattern (`D109B_*_MISSING` precedent). I found no infeasible fixture assumption (memory seeding controls `seedObjectState`/`seedBlob`/`markPromoted` exist for the publicly-uncompletable memory model) and no missing causal mutant: wrong-but-countable pair, surviving branch, extra row, dangling post-state, count-mismatch rollbacks, shared/cross-object blob retention, and partial-replay poisons are all rostered.\n\n**8–9. Scope — preserved.** Two GREEN batches, retained/source-pin/custody gates, and explicit stop/reslice triggers are enumerated; nothing requires or authorizes schema, reverse index, facade, dependency, threshold, workload, protocol/wire/digest/QC/adoption/availability, product API, runtime reclamation, D.109d, cross-database authority, or a campaign. The no-head floor rewrite reuses the existing `ExpectedHead` variant already encodable by the v1 codecs and accepted at genesis.\n\nNon-blocking P2 observations only: the receipt's `deletedBlobDigests` discloses digests not present in the request (metadata, not bytes, and explicitly required for the human-verifiable outcome); the memory maintenance path is exercisable only through package-internal seeding (inherent to the honest ephemeral model, already budgeted as \"memory test control\").\n\nVERDICT: APPROVED\n\nP0_P1_UNION: none\n\nD109C_RED_MAY_START: yes"}]}
