has exactly those twelve members.\n- **Node four-table authority** — `create-scaffold.ts:76-100`, `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON` (`:763`), WAL/FULL (`:785-786`), `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` (`:246`). The plan's delete order (promotions → generations → blobs, `slices/02:177-183`) is exactly FK-correct against `promotions`' two foreign keys (`:97-98`).\n- **Browser v3 / nine-store / four AHE stores, no reverse index** — `schema-idb.ts:60-71`; `indexNames.length !== 0` is rejected (`:177`), blobs keyed by `digest` alone (`:21-22`). Same for SQLite `blobs(digest PRIMARY KEY)`.\n- **Exact D.109a AHE subset** — `ClosedEpochCleanupPlan` (`closed-epoch-cleanup.ts:34-56`) is the plan's captured input plus `issuance`; every field name matches.\n- **Rollback order / floor** — `rollbackGenerationIds: [first, second]`, `floor: second` (`:336-341`); `deleteGenerationIds` is lexicographically `.sort()`ed (`:337`), so ancestry-driven rebuild is mandatory, not stylistic.\n- **The parent-presence defect is real, with exactly two predicates** — `creator-adoption.ts:211-217` and `creator-adoption-commit.ts:215-221`. Both reject a `present` base whose parent row is absent, and both accept `{kind:\"none\"}` unconditionally. The \"both creator parent-presence predicates are source pins\" claim is accurate.\n- **Floor normalization is safe for every reader found** — `recoverActiveGeneration` verifies only the adopted generation (`transition.ts:407-462`); `reopenCreatorSuccessorMaterial` reads `presentBase` of active and first rollback only, never the floor (`creator-adoption.ts:906-926`); `v3-live.ts:1666-1696` only inspects `Adopted|Complete|Staged`. `closureDigest` derives from the closure alone (`codecs.ts:65-73`), so re-encoding preserves it; both codecs are root exports (`storage/src/index.ts:1-6`).\n- **Later-epoch plannability survives** — replaying `lineagePlan`'s prefix walk (`:300-319`) against a post-normalization graph terminates cleanly at the normalized floor. The AHE analogue of D.109b's watermark problem needs no extra state.\n- **`Complete`/`Adopted`/`Superseded` really do imply complete promotion sets** — `transition.ts:373`; the `Staged`/`Discarded` carve-out is correct.\n- **RED is structurally executable** — D.109b's roster is the same shape minus the worker. Readiness gating is filesystem source inspection, not module resolution (`storage-node/tests/phase-6b-issuance-retention-red.test.ts:31-37`), and candidates load by file URL, never package subpath (`tests/phase-6b-issuance-retention-red.test.ts:47-49`) — no TS2307, no resolution failure. Browser token injection via esbuild virtual module (`phase-6b-issuance-retention-global-setup.ts:5-30`); the pw file hosts its own server inline; two-entry-point worker bundling and edge-termination are precedented (`phase-2e6-global-setup.ts:12-25`).\n- **Registry identity is implementable as described** — `node-issuance-store.ts:1075-1151` is the precedent, with copy/proxy/cross-backend denial already exercised. One construction site each: `create-scaffold.ts:858`, `idb-adapter.ts:971`.\n- **Requirement 9 holds** — no schema, reverse index, facade member, product/runtime API, dependency, threshold, workload, protocol/wire/digest/QC/adoption/availability change, or cross-database authority is demonstrably required.\n\n## P1\n\n### Memory owner cannot reach the adopted/superseded state its frozen positive control and `TransitionOwner` mutation require\n\nThe plan treats memory as a full peer backend running all ten steps (`slices/02:145-146`, `:275-278`), asserts memory \"owns … promotion evidence in one synchronous `TransitionOwner`\" (`:28-29`), freezes a \"genuine five-generation positive control\" (`:241-244`), and states the focused Vitest selection covers \"the shared/memory and genuine Node owners\" (`:228-229`).\n\nThe shipped memory store cannot reach that state:\n\n- `packages/storage/src/memory.ts:32` — `new TransitionOwner(\"ephemeral\")`.\n- `transition.ts:343` — `if (this.durability === \"ephemeral\") return rejected(\"DURABILITY_UNAVAILABLE\")` in `promoteReference`.\n- `transition.ts:373-374` — `completeGeneration` requires those promotions.\n- `transition.ts:524` — `swapHead` requires `state === \"Complete\"`.\n\nThe source says so itself: `memory.ts:114`, `:130`, and `:144` (\"Can only adopt a Complete candidate, which memory cannot create publicly\").\n\nSo the memory head is permanently `{kind:\"none\"}` and no memory row can ever be `Adopted` or `Superseded`. Since the closed input requires a `present` `expectedHead` (`slices/02:85-86`) and step 3 requires active `Adopted` plus two `Superseded` ancestors (`:152-156`), **every well-formed `reclaimClosedEpoch` call against the shipped memory facade must fail at step 1 with `AHE_RECLAMATION_RETRY_REQUIRED`.** The frozen positive control is infeasible on that owner, and GREEN batch 1's `TransitionOwner` deletion mutation would ship unreachable from any exported facade.\n\nUnlike D.109b there is no ready seam. D.109b's shared RED drove a seedable ephemeral store from the **pre-existing** `@ts-drp/issuance-store/conformance` subpath (`tests/phase-6b-issuance-retention-red.test.ts:29,39,46-50`). `@ts-drp/storage` has no conformance subpath — exports are `.`, `./contract`, `./adapter`, `./snapshot-transfer` (`packages/storage/package.json:17-34`) — and `./contract` exports only `StoreContractFactory`, `STORE_CONTRACT_SCENARIOS`, `runStoreContract` (`contract.ts:15,17,421`), with no seeding. The only strict owner is `createTransitionHarness()` at `packages/storage/tests/internal-harness.ts:7`, a package **test** file, not an export, returning a raw `TransitionOwner` rather than an `AheDurableStore` facade — so a facade-keyed registry cannot resolve it.\n\n**Smallest correction** (no new package surface, no facade change, no runtime change, roster paths unchanged):\n\n1. In §\"Source audit and one-owner seam\", replace the memory sentence with the fact that `createMemoryAheDurableStore` is `TransitionOwne